            <ArticleTitle>Comparative evaluation of the efficacy of two modes of delivery of Piroxicam (Dolonex(®)) for the management of postendodontic pain: A randomized control trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0972-0707.186454</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Alleviating pain is of utmost importance when treating patients with endodontic pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To compare and evaluate the efficacy of two modes of delivery of pretreatment Piroxicam (Dolonex(®), Pfizer) for the management of postendodontic pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Sixty-six patients with symptomatic irreversible pulpitis were randomly divided into three groups of 22 subjects Group I - control group, no pharmacological intervention, Group II - patients received pretreatment oral Piroxicam (40 mg), Group III - patients received pretreatment intraligamentary injections totaling 0.4 mL of Piroxicam. Single visit endodontic therapy was performed by a single endodontist. Visual analogue scale was used to record pain before treatment and 4, 8, 12, 24, and 48 h postoperatively. Mann-Whitney U-test and Kruskal-Wallis tests were used to analyze the data.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The patients in Groups II and III perceived less postendodontic pain as compared to Group I (P &lt; 0.05), at all the time intervals. At 12, 24, and 48 h, pain experience in patients of Group III was significantly less.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Intraligamentary mode of delivery of Piroxicam was more efficacious.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
